# XSH posix_fadvise()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# posix_fadvise() is the Advisory Information option (ADV). The advice has no
# observable effect that the text requires, so the assertions check return
# values, errors, and that the file is left as it was. Errors are returned,
# not stored in errno.

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.001
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_fadvise() on a regular file open for reading returns 0
           for each of POSIX_FADV_NORMAL, SEQUENTIAL, RANDOM, WILLNEED,
           DONTNEED, NOREUSE, with offset 0 and len 0, and with a range
           wholly beyond the end of the file.
test       t/001-advice-values.c

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.002
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       After posix_fadvise() calls with every advice value (some with
           POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED), the file still has the same length and
           contents, the file offset of the descriptor is unchanged, and a
           write through the descriptor is read back correctly.
test       t/002-no-effect.c

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.003
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_fadvise() on -1 and on a closed descriptor returns EBADF.
test       t/003-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.004
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_fadvise() with an advice value equal to none of the six
           constants returns EINVAL.
test       t/004-einval-advice.c

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.005
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_fadvise() with len -1 and a valid advice on a regular
           file returns EINVAL.
test       t/005-einval-len.c

assertion  XSH.posix_fadvise.006
anchor     functions/posix_fadvise.html#ERRORS/ESPIPE
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_fadvise() on both ends of a pipe and on a FIFO returns
           ESPIPE.
test       t/006-espipe.c
